The '''Corsair Cove Dungeon''' is a large cave system beneath the [[Corsair Cove]] at the southern part of [[Feldip Hills]]. It is mainly inhabited by [[ogresses]], though the western caves are part of the [[Myths' Guild]]. 
The [[Dwarf multicannon]] can be used in the dungeon, though it is not [[multicombat]].

==Transportation==
{{Map|x:2523,y:2861|mapID=0|align=right|caption=Location of the Corsair Cove Dungeon}}
* Talk to [[Cabin Boy Colin]] on the western end of [[Rimmington]] after completion of [[The Corsair Curse]], or [[Captain Tock]] during the quest. This is the only way to access the island in [[free-to-play]] worlds.
* [[Spirit tree]] teleport to Feldip Hills and run east.
* [[Charter ship]] to Corsair Cove.
* [[Mythical cape]] teleport to the [[Myths' Guild]].

==Layout==
===Eastern side===
The eastern side of the dungeon is accessible to all players. It only contains [[Ogress Warrior]]s, [[Ogress Shaman]]s, and a few [[Spider]]s.

To the east is the [[ogress]]es' bank vault, which serves as scenery. [[Francois]], [[Arsen]]'s brother, can be seen digging towards the vault, with the ogresses none the wiser.

To the north-west is a [[Corsair Cove Resource Area|mining site]], which requires completion of [[Dragon Slayer I]] to access. Players can access the site from the dungeon north of the bridge, which requires level 15 in [[Agility]] to use. Before the shortcut can be used, you must speak to [[Haris]] to gain access to the [[Corsair Cove Resource Area]]. This site has five [[Coal rocks|coal]], two [[Mithril rocks|mithril]], and one [[adamantite rock]].

In this area, there are spawns of [[bread]], [[raw shrimps]], [[burnt shrimp]], [[rope]], [[spade]], as well as some cages with [[gold bar|gold bars]] and [[gold necklace|gold necklaces]] which can be [[Telekinetic Grab|telegrabbed]].

